# Agent guardrails

This project follows the Go conventions recorded under `.agents/rules/` —
read every `*.mdc` file there before making changes. They cover things a
generic Go style guide won't: this project's specific footguns, SQL
column-ordering conventions, where a domain's files must live, and similar
project-specific rules.

When adding a new domain, prefer `goforge generate domain <name> --fields ...`
over hand-writing one — it keeps the vertical-slice shape (model, service,
repository, HTTP handler, tests) and the wiring in `cmd/api/main.go`
consistent with every other domain in this project.
